# MaCSad public research digest

This public template is evidence-first and intentionally static in posture. A later
sealed publication batch will supply reviewed records; this baseline never exposes
the private workspace or implies that example content is a discovery.

## To publicationVisible (evidenceComplete: Bool, approvalGranted: Bool) -> Bool:
    If evidenceComplete:
        Return approvalGranted.
    Return false.

## Component MacsAdPublic:
    Let topic be a signal "All".
    Let pipelineSteps be ["Question", "Attempt", "Evidence", "Review", "Publication"].
    View:
        css r"* { box-sizing: border-box; } .public-shell { min-height: 100vh; color: #172b35; background: #f5f2e9; font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif; } .masthead { padding: 22px clamp(22px,5vw,72px); color: #f8f4e8; background: #102c3b; border-bottom: 1px solid #274b59; } .masthead-inner { max-width: 1240px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 24px; margin: auto; } .wordmark { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; } .wordmark strong { font: 780 20px/1 Georgia, serif; letter-spacing: -.02em; } .wordmark span { color: #afc3cb; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .1em; text-transform: uppercase; } .seal { padding: 7px 10px; color: #d8ff72; border: 1px solid rgba(216,255,114,.38); border-radius: 999px; font: 700 10px/1 ui-monospace, monospace; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; } .hero { padding: clamp(64px,9vw,118px) clamp(22px,5vw,72px) 72px; background: radial-gradient(circle at 85% 15%,rgba(216,255,114,.14),transparent 30%), #102c3b; } .hero-inner { max-width: 1240px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1.35fr) minmax(280px,.65fr); gap: clamp(40px,7vw,100px); align-items: end; margin: auto; } .overline { margin: 0 0 18px; color: #d8ff72; font: 800 11px/1 ui-monospace, monospace; letter-spacing: .15em; text-transform: uppercase; } h1 { max-width: 800px; margin: 0; color: #f9f6ed; font: 700 clamp(44px,7vw,86px)/.98 Georgia, serif; letter-spacing: -.045em; } .hero-copy { max-width: 680px; margin: 24px 0 0; color: #b9cbd1; font-size: clamp(15px,1.6vw,18px); line-height: 1.7; } .issue-card { padding: 25px; color: #1a333e; background: #d8ff72; border-radius: 16px; box-shadow: 0 22px 70px rgba(0,0,0,.18); } .issue-card small { display: block; margin-bottom: 28px; font: 800 10px/1 ui-monospace, monospace; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; } .issue-card strong { display: block; font: 750 31px/1.05 Georgia, serif; } .issue-card p { margin: 12px 0 0; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.55; } .content { max-width: 1240px; margin: auto; padding: 58px clamp(22px,5vw,72px) 90px; } .section-head { display: flex; align-items: end; justify-content: space-between; gap: 24px; margin-bottom: 24px; } .section-head h2 { margin: 0; color: #123342; font: 730 clamp(28px,4vw,42px)/1.05 Georgia, serif; letter-spacing: -.025em; } .section-head p { max-width: 520px; margin: 0; color: #69767c; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; } .filters { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; margin: 24px 0; } .filter { padding: 8px 12px; color: #34505c; background: transparent; border: 1px solid #c9c6bc; border-radius: 999px; font: 700 11px/1 inherit; cursor: pointer; } .filter:hover { color: #f8f4e8; background: #153c4b; border-color: #153c4b; } .feature-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1.5fr) minmax(260px,.5fr); gap: 16px; } .research-card { padding: clamp(24px,4vw,42px); background: #fffdf8; border: 1px solid #d7d2c6; border-radius: 17px; box-shadow: 0 14px 42px rgba(16,44,59,.06); } .record-line { display: flex; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 25px; } .badge { padding: 6px 8px; color: #12687a; background: #e4f2f3; border-radius: 6px; font: 800 9px/1 ui-monospace, monospace; letter-spacing: .1em; text-transform: uppercase; } .badge-muted { color: #6e685c; background: #eee9dd; } .research-card h3 { max-width: 760px; margin: 0; color: #183440; font: 720 clamp(25px,3.5vw,42px)/1.12 Georgia, serif; letter-spacing: -.025em; } .abstract { margin: 20px 0 0; color: #5c696f; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.75; } .evidence { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit,minmax(150px,1fr)); gap: 10px; margin-top: 30px; } .evidence-item { padding: 14px; background: #f2efe7; border-radius: 10px; } .evidence-item span { display: block; color: #758087; font-size: 10px; } .evidence-item strong { display: block; margin-top: 6px; color: #263d48; font-size: 12px; } .notice { margin-top: 25px; padding: 15px; color: #5d5648; background: #faf4df; border-left: 3px solid #d9a72e; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6; } .rail { padding: 24px; color: #eaf0ef; background: #173d4b; border-radius: 17px; } .rail h3 { margin: 0 0 18px; font: 700 18px/1.2 Georgia, serif; } .pipeline { margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; } .pipeline li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 25px 1fr; gap: 10px; align-items: center; padding: 11px 0; color: #b9cbd1; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.1); font-size: 12px; } .step { width: 22px; height: 22px; display: grid; place-items: center; color: #d8ff72; border: 1px solid rgba(216,255,114,.42); border-radius: 999px; font: 700 9px/1 ui-monospace, monospace; } .principles { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit,minmax(220px,1fr)); gap: 12px; margin-top: 50px; } .principle { padding: 19px; border-top: 2px solid #163e4d; background: rgba(255,255,255,.42); } .principle strong { display: block; margin-bottom: 8px; color: #173642; font-size: 13px; } .principle p { margin: 0; color: #6d787e; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6; } .footer { padding: 28px clamp(22px,5vw,72px); color: #8da0a8; background: #0c2632; font-size: 11px; } .footer-inner { max-width: 1240px; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 20px; margin: auto; } @media (max-width: 820px) { .wordmark span { display: none; } .hero-inner, .feature-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .section-head { align-items: start; flex-direction: column; } .footer-inner { flex-direction: column; } }"
        css ".masthead-inner, .section-head, .footer-inner { flex-wrap: wrap; } .hero-inner, .feature-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(280px,100%),1fr)); } .section-head > * { flex: 1 1 300px; }"
        div [class="public-shell"]:
            header [class="masthead"]:
                div [class="masthead-inner"]:
                    div [class="wordmark"]:
                        strong: "MaCSad"
                        span: "Public research record"
                    span [class="seal"]: "Evidence first"
            section [class="hero"]:
                div [class="hero-inner"]:
                    div:
                        p [class="overline"]: "Mathematics × computer science"
                        h1: "Discovery should be inspectable."
                        p [class="hero-copy"]: "MaCSad is a framework for directed auto-research. Questions become controlled processes; claims become public only after their evidence and review trail are sealed."
                    aside [class="issue-card"]:
                        small: "Baseline edition · 001"
                        strong: "No discoveries published yet."
                        p: "This is the honest empty state while the research and publication pipelines are being connected."
            main [class="content"]:
                div [class="section-head"]:
                    h2: "The research ledger"
                    p: "Browse reviewed outputs without inheriting the private control plane. Every future record will cite its source snapshot, evidence, verifier, and publication decision."
                div [class="filters"]:
                    button [class="filter"]:
                        on click:
                            Set topic to "All".
                        span: "All"
                    button [class="filter"]:
                        on click:
                            Set topic to "Mathematics".
                        span: "Mathematics"
                    button [class="filter"]:
                        on click:
                            Set topic to "Computer science".
                        span: "Computer science"
                    button [class="filter"]:
                        on click:
                            Set topic to "Methods".
                        span: "Methods"
                div [class="feature-grid"]:
                    article [class="research-card"]:
                        div [class="record-line"]:
                            span [class="badge"]: "Selected: {topic}"
                            span [class="badge badge-muted"]: "Template record"
                        h3: "A publication slot reserved for the first reviewed result."
                        p [class="abstract"]: "When the sealed batch is enabled, this card will be generated from approved publication records—not from live administrative data and never directly from an agent chat."
                        div [class="evidence"]:
                            div [class="evidence-item"]:
                                span: "Source snapshot"
                                strong: "Required"
                            div [class="evidence-item"]:
                                span: "Evidence bundle"
                                strong: "Required"
                            div [class="evidence-item"]:
                                span: "Independent review"
                                strong: "Required"
                            div [class="evidence-item"]:
                                span: "Decision record"
                                strong: "Required"
                        div [class="notice"]: "Example only · this template is not a scientific claim and contains no generated research output."
                    aside [class="rail"]:
                        h3: "Path to publication"
                        ol [class="pipeline"]:
                            for each step in pipelineSteps:
                                li:
                                    span [class="step"]: "·"
                                    span: "{step}"
                div [class="principles"]:
                    div [class="principle"]:
                        strong: "Repository grounded"
                        p: "Every campaign operates on an immutable snapshot of a watched GitHub workspace."
                    div [class="principle"]:
                        strong: "Process controlled"
                        p: "Roles and decisions move through explicit, inspectable control-flow states."
                    div [class="principle"]:
                        strong: "Fail closed"
                        p: "Missing evidence or approval means a record is not eligible for publication."
                    div [class="principle"]:
                        strong: "Batch separated"
                        p: "The public site is generated from a sealed export, away from private operations."
            footer [class="footer"]:
                div [class="footer-inner"]:
                    span: "MaCSad · Brahmastra Labs"
                    span: "Baseline template · no production data"

## Test: Publication visibility is fail closed
    Let completeAndApproved be publicationVisible(true, true).
    Let completeNotApproved be publicationVisible(true, false).
    Let incompleteApproved be publicationVisible(false, true).
    Let incompleteNotApproved be publicationVisible(false, false).
    Expect that completeAndApproved is equal to true.
    Expect that completeNotApproved is equal to false.
    Expect that incompleteApproved is equal to false.
    Expect that incompleteNotApproved is equal to false.
    For all booleans evidenceComplete and approvalGranted:
        Let visible be publicationVisible(evidenceComplete, approvalGranted).
        If visible:
            Expect that evidenceComplete is equal to true.
            Expect that approvalGranted is equal to true.

## Main
Render:
    css "html, body, #root { width: 100%; min-height: 100%; } body { max-width: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }"
Mount MacsAdPublic at "#root".
